  {
    "index": 7,
    "title": "Training and inference use different information",
    "speaker": "Niels",
    "seconds": 55,
    "notes": "Explicitly answer the potential leakage question. Future Exo frames are privileged supervision during training; they are not passed to the deployed forecaster. Test inputs remain language, past Ego RGB and past hand states. This resembles learning with privileged information. The targets may nevertheless encourage reliance on temporal alignment or dataset regularities, motivating controls. Hand off: Emiel will explain how the predicted Exo features improve pose predictions.",
    "source": "§3.1–3.4",
    "el": [
