  {
    "index": 8,
    "title": "GLMM refines poses globally, then locally",
    "speaker": "Emiel",
    "seconds": 85,
    "notes": "Global modulation derives scale, shift and residual weights from one reconstructed clip vector, plus cross-attention. Local modulation cross-attends over predicted frame features, then uses a learned gate and adaptive normalization. Soft alignment accommodates imperfect temporal correspondence. The normalized pose features become (1+gamma) times LN(x) plus beta. Do not say that attention alone proves geometric understanding.",
    "source": "Fig.3; §3.4, Eqs.16–22",
    "el": [
      {
